[agent] How it was done:
[agent] - Uploaded both CSVs and an analysis script to the project's dataset storage via the Hopsworks dataset API, then ran the analysis as a Hopsworks Python job (`skew_detect`) on the cluster. The job joined training and serving rows on `entity_id`, computed per-feature absolute differences (f1, f2, f3, f5 had zero difference; f4 diverged on every row), confirmed `f4_train == log1p(f4_serve)` to ~2.5e-07 mean absolute error, and wrote `answers.json` into the project dataset. I then read it back through the dataset API into `submission/answers.json`.
[agent] Two environment quirks worth noting: the `NO_PROXY=10.0.0.0/8` env var made the SDK bypass the mandatory localhost proxy (fixed by overriding `NO_PROXY` per command), and direct feature-group inserts were impossible because the client writes straight to HopsFS on port 8020, which only HTTPS-proxied traffic could not reach — hence the remote-job approach. Also, inside the job the dataset REST download reported "Path not found" for existing files; reading from the `/hopsfs` mount worked instead.
